      "text": "To find the vector on the line at \\( t = -7 \\), we need to determine the parametric equation of the line. The parametric equation of a line is given by:\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{r}(t) = \\mathbf{r}_0 + t \\mathbf{d}\n\\]\n\nwhere \\(\\mathbf{r}_0\\) is a point on the line and \\(\\mathbf{d}\\) is the direction vector of the line.\n\nGiven:\n- When \\( t = 2 \\), \\(\\mathbf{r}(2) = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 4 \\end{pmatrix}\\).\n- When \\( t = 3 \\), \\(\\mathbf{r}(3) = \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ -4 \\end{pmatrix}\\).\n\nFirst, we find the direction vector \\(\\mathbf{d}\\). The direction vector \\(\\mathbf{d}\\) can be found by subtracting the vector at \\( t = 2 \\) from the vector at \\( t = 3 \\):\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{d} = \\mathbf{r}(3) - \\mathbf{r}(2) = \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ -4 \\end{pmatrix} - \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 4 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 3 - 1 \\\\ -4 - 4 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ -8 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nSo, the direction vector is \\(\\mathbf{d} = \\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ -8 \\end{pmatrix}\\).\n\nNext, we need to determine the point \\(\\mathbf{r}_0\\). When \\( t = 2 \\), we have:\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{r}(2) = \\mathbf{r}_0 + 2 \\mathbf{d} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 4 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nSubstituting the direction vector \\(\\mathbf{d} = \\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ -8 \\end{pmatrix}\\):\n\n\\[\n\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 4 \\end{pmatrix} = \\mathbf{r}_0 + 2 \\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ -8 \\end{pmatrix} = \\mathbf{r}_0 + \\begin{pmatrix} 4 \\\\ -16 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nSolving for \\(\\mathbf{r}_0\\):\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{r}_0 = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 4 \\end{pmatrix} - \\begin{pmatrix} 4 \\\\ -16 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 - 4 \\\\ 4 + 16 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 20 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nNow, we have the parametric equation of the line:\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{r}(t) = \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 20 \\end{pmatrix} + t \\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ -8 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nTo find the vector on the line at \\( t = -7 \\):\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{r}(-7) = \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 20 \\end{pmatrix} + (-7) \\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ -8 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 20 \\end{pmatrix} + \\begin{pmatrix} -14 \\\\ 56 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} -3 - 14 \\\\ 20 + 56 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} -17 \\\\ 76 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nThus, the vector on the line at \\( t = -7 \\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\begin{pmatrix} -17 \\\\ 76 \\end{pmatrix}}\n\\]",
